                    "text": "The proposed agricultural appropriations bill slashes critical food assistance while failing to address systemic waste. Hawaii\u2019s food insecurity crisis\u2014170k residents monthly relying on aid\u2014isn\u2019t solved by cutting SNAP funding by $290B over a decade to offset tax breaks for the ultrawealthy.\n\nThe real issue? Bureaucrats prioritize foreign aid and redundant programs over streamlining existing systems. Redirect that $2.3M USDA cut to audit bloated contracts, eliminate redundant admin layers, and enforce strict accountability for every dollar spent.\n\nVulnerable families shouldn\u2019t pay for D.C.\u2019s refusal to fix broken processes.\n\nSee how the numbers and policy failures stack up\u2014full details here: https://t.co/EMn6eJ08vI",
