                    "text": "The USDA\u2019s refusal to release $5B in SNAP contingency funds during a shutdown isn\u2019t fiscal prudence\u2014it\u2019s political cruelty. Biden-era reserves exist precisely to prevent hunger crises, yet bureaucrats weaponize delays to pressure Congress. While Rep. Case scrambles for state-level fixes, the real issue is D.C.\u2019s addiction to holding vulnerable Americans hostage.\n\nVeterans, seniors, and disabled citizens shouldn\u2019t starve because agencies hoard taxpayer-funded reserves as leverage. Trump\u2019s DOGE already exposed $175B in waste; redirecting a fraction of that could secure SNAP instantly.\n\nThis isn\u2019t about budgets\u2014it\u2019s about bureaucrats prioritizing power over people.\n\nThe receipts on who\u2019s blocking relief and why are public\u2014see the evidence: https://t.co/2KfDfFBI6p",
